        <p>DR.J. COLLIS BROWNE'S CHLORODYNE. THE ORIGINAL AND ONLY GENUINE. CfiLORODYNE is admitted by the Profession to be the most wonderful and valual?le remedy ever dis Covered. CHLORODYNE is tbe best remedy known for Coughs, Consumption, Bronchitis and Asthma. CIILORODYNE effectually checks and arrests those too often fatal diseases—Diphtheria, Fever, Croup, Ague. CHLORODYNE acts like a charm in Diarrhoea and is the only specific in Cholera and Dysentery. CULORODYNE effectually cuts short all attacks of Epilepsy, Hysteria, Palpitation, and Spasms. VIILORODYNE is the only palliative in Neural- k../ ea, Rheumatism, Gout, Cancer, Toothache, Meningitis, Ac. From Dr. B. J. BoULToN AND CO., Horncastle. We have made pretty extensive use of Chlorodyne moor practice lately and look upon it as an excellent direct Seda- tive and Anti-spasmodic. It seems to allay pain and irrita- tion in whatever organ, and from whatever cause. It induces a feeling of comfort and quietude not obtainable by any other remedy, and it seems to possess this great advantage over all other sedatives ; that it leaves no unpleasant after effects. 1 " Earl Russell communicated to the College of Physicians that he received a despatch from her Majesty's Consul at blanilla to the effect that Cholera had been raging fearfully, and that the ONLY remedy of any service was CHLORO- DYNE."—See Lancet, Ist December, 1864. CAUTION.—BEWARE OF PIRACY AND IMITA- %IONS. CAUTIoN.—Vice-Chancellor Sir W. PAGE WOOD stated that tr. J. Comas BnoWNE was, undoubtedly, the inventor of LORODYNE " and that the story of the defendant FREEmix, was deliberately untrue, which he regretted to say had been sworn to.—See Times, 13th July, 1864. Sold ih bottles at is. Itid., 2s. 9c1., and 4s. 6d. None is genuine without the words " DR. J COLLIS BROWNE'S CHLORODYNE "on the Government Stamp. Overwhelm- ing Medics 'testimony accompanies each bottle. SOLE MANUFACTURERS :—J. T. DAVRNPORT, 33, Great Russell-street, Bloomsbury, LOn4On</p>
