        <p>RAILWAY ACCIDENT AT WILDERSPOOL CROSSING.</p>
        <p>DELAY OF TRAFFIC.</p>
        <p>An accident occurred on the London and North Western low level railway at Warrington on Friday morning at a quarter to seven which caused great dislocation of traffic between 'Warrington and Man- chester. It appears that a short goods train, con- taicing a 25 ton wire rope which was being taken from Whiiecross works to a siding near Blackbear Bridge, thence to be sent on to the Ship Canal had got nearly to the gate of the crossing when one of the wheels of a wagon lett the line, through a mishap to an axle. As the point where this accident happened was on the highway from Warrington into Cheshire, all vehicular traffic was stopped for about an hour, causing much inconvenience to the residents in Stockton Heath and surrounding districts. The permanent way was torn up for some yards by the accident, the wagon finally leaving the rails. Mr. Starkey, stationmaster, Bank Quay, and Mr. Mar- shall, were soon on the spot after the accident and by the aid of two locomotives the waggon was dragged across the roadway to the Arpley side of the crossings, and a breakdown gang arrived to re- pair the rails snd to remove the obstruction. Pas- senger traffic on the railway for a time was taken by a single line, but it was found necessary to pro- cure a large crane, which blocked the line alto- gether for two or threa hours, but by one o'clock the rails were cleared.</p>
