        <head>SMITH.</head>
        <p>SMITH.</p>
        <p>The reason Mr Smith was advised at Charinc Cross Hospital to t are an emulsion of cod-liver oil, is because an emulsion is much more effectual and more practical in every way than the plain oil. Where plain oil will tar digestion, a perfect emulsion will be a positive aid t o it; and wkere plain oil will pass through the system without being absorbed, a irriect emulsion will be readily takes into the blood, where it can do its work in building up the system.</p>
        <p>We have no hesitation in dezlaring positively that Scott's Emulsioo is the only pethc emulsion of cod- liver oil in the world. Bsiides tois oil, Scott's Emul- sion contains glycerine and hypophosphites, both of which serve an admirable purpose in building up the system. There is a wide difforence between aa emulsion of cod-liver oil and a mixture of oil with other ingredients, and the proof that Scott's Emul- sion is a pnrfect emulsion is found in the fact that it retains its emulsifiel form indefinitely, whereas other emulsions soon svarato, the oil in them rising to the top of the bottle.</p>
        <p>Scott's Emulsion is perfectly palatable, an aid to digestion, a specific for thruat and lung complaints and is the bost known remedy to give vital strength!' to the entira system and,pr3mote the making of healthy flash. For sale by all chemists. You may obtain a sample of Sc3tt's. Emulsion by sending threepence to cover postage to Scott and Bowne, Limited, Manufacturing Chemists, 95 ,Great Saffron Hall, London, 8.C., and mentioning this paper.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-01-20_WidnesExaminer_art0042" n="art0042">
        <head>I PARR'S BANK LIMITED.</head>
        <p>I PARR'S BANK LIMITED.</p>
        <p>ANNUAL MEETING.</p>
        <p>The Annual meeting of Pares Bank, Ltd., was held at Cannon-street Hotel, London. yesterday. The following is a eopy of the annual report of the directors.</p>
        <p>The directors in submittincv to the shareholders this balance sheet of the Bank at 31st December, 1893, certi- fied by the auditors, have to report that the position and prospects of the business continue to be in every way satisfactory. The amalgamation of the Derb7 and Derbyshire Bank- ing Company Limited, wi.';ts tlais company has been suc- cessfully carried out. The subscribt-d capital has been in- creased to £6,850,000 ; the paid-up capital to £1,370,000 and the reserve fund to £1,370,000. Including £63,149 lOs 9d brought forwazd at 30th June, 1898, the net balance of profits, alter providing for all bad and doubt- ful debts, and rebating the current bills at 5 per cent.,is £209,920 18s. 4d, ; from this sum the directors recom- mend a dividend at the rate of 19 per cent, per annum, free of income tax, for the quarter ended 31st December. 1898,t0 be payable Gfla Ist February, £65.075; a dividend at the same rate for the quarter ending3lst Mar 6,1898, to be payable on Ist May, '1899, to the shareholders whose names shall be on the regis.er on 13th April. £65,075; the transfer to bank premiss account £15,000; total. £145,150 ; leaving balance to be carried to next account £64,770 18Q. 4.</p>
        <p>, . Branches ot the bank have been opened at I,FinsbulT Square, E.C. ; 2, Grand Parade,High,tate, N. ; Fairfield, Liverpool; Upper Brighton, CuestUre; and Nantwich, Cheshire.</p>
        <p>Mr. R. 0. Yeats, formerly general manager of the Alliance Bank Limited, and latcerly manager at Bar- tholomew-lane, has retired.and the direc :ors desire to re- cord their appreciation of his long and valuable services. The directors who retire at this time by rotation are Mr. Edward BAnbury, Mr. Alfred Crewdsoa, Sir S. .1. Harwood, Mr. Emil Heinemann, Mr. Robert Neill, jun., Mr. James Tullocu and Mr. A. M. Turner, all of whorls are eligible for re-election. The aud:tors, Messrs. Turquand, Youn7s, Bishop and Clarke, Lqn.lon, Messrs. Steri, Tavhr and Stead, Liver- pool, and Mos,v. Edwin Collier, Tongue and Co., Mm.. cheater, alio rttire, and offer themselves for re-election.. CECIL F. PARR, Chairman. 4, dartholomew-lane. L 'ndon, E. C., 13th January, 1899.</p>
