        <p>ESTABLISH ED 1824. Sold by Chemtsta throughout the Worlds HOCKEY. STOCKTON HEATH V. Moss SIDE. These teams met for the first time on Saturday the game being played on the around of the Warrington Cricket Club. The early portion of the game was unin- terestieg, the ball being constantly placed over the side lines, but afterwards some spirited play way witnessed, and Stockton Heath obtained a corner, this being safely cleared by the visitors. Tbe home team forwards again pressed, and a shot by Gardiner gained the first point in the game. At half-time Stockton Heath led by one goal to none. On resuming the visitor? forwards mace a series of attacks on the home goal, and W. Bamford placed Moss Side on level terms. The remaining portion of the game was evenly contested, but nothing further was scored, the match ending in a draw. Moss SIDE " A " v. STOCKTON HEATH "A." Played at Chorlton-cum-Hardy on Saturday. Stockton Heath arrived two men short, but a substitute being found them it was arranged to play ten aside. Moss Side preesed from the bully off, and eventually ran out winners of a plearant but one-sided game by seven goals to nil. Burns (three), Dickson (two), and Johnson (two) were the scorers for Moss Side, whilst the visiting goal- keeper was the only one of- his side to show up at all well. ALTRINCHAM V. LATCHFORD. This match was played at Latchford on Saturday,and a poor game resu.ted in a draw of two goals each. The ground being in a very uneven state scientific hockey was quite out ot the question. Altrincham were greatly handicapped through only having ten men.</p>
