        <p>Serummaging on the Swinton line end el in Briers scor- ing a try, Dale failing to add a zeal from an easy place. , Keeping up the pr .ssure, Se Helens te•ted the visiting I defenders, and Taylor ultimately scored a second try for St. Helens near the corner, the same player failing to pl ace a goal. Lewis, of Swinton, eisei the pressure by a seleedid rue to the home 25, bit Foulkes brought him down, and again play was taken to the Swinton quarter. Towards the Close Pearson pissed to Valentine, who, reundieg his men, scorsi a splendid try nesr the posts, and added a geel fr•-m t le, place Result :--St. Heieus, two ties ; S vinten. oIA goal and ole try BROUGHTON RANGERS V. ROCHDALE HORNETS* The Ringers had a poor team at Broughton, and the , Flornets won an exciting contest by a dropped goal to nil. Wg; gained the point in the second half. TYLDESLEY v. OLDHAM. This match at Tyldesley was a runaway affair for O'd- ham, who ran up the big score of three goals and nine tries to one dropped goal. Williams (three), Martin.and Lees were among the scorers for Oldham ; France ob. taire I the losers' only point. MORECAMBE v. SALFORD. . An excellent game resulted at Morecambe Salford won by one goal and two tries to nil. Pearson played fine'y, and s. cure I both tries. YORKSHIRE SENIOR COMPETITION. LIVERSEDGE v. HECKMONDWIKE. A. capital game was witnessed, at Liversedge. The visitors had a little the better of matters, but no scoring took place, the result being a pointless draw. BRIGFIOUSE RANGERS v. LEEDS P kRISH CHURCH. Tnis mach came off at Brighouse. . and was won by the visit ers by two tries to nil. Smith played pro- minently and obtained the tries. BATLEY v. CaSTLEFORD. The local men had matters all their own way at Bat- ley, and won by one goal and six tries to nil. Oak- land (three), D avics, Gate and Geodall were the try- getters. HUNSLET v. LEEDS. Fully 10,000 people viewed this contest at Hunslet. The result Was a victory for the home fifteen by three goals (two dropped) and one try to nil. Albert Gold- thorpe played brilliantly, and did all the scoring. WAKEFIELD TRINITY v. BRADFORD. The Trinitarians, although playing on their own ground, suffered defeat, Bradford winning by three goals and two tries to one goal one try. Booth, Cooper. and Word were the scorers for Bradford ; Metcalf and Walton &amp;jog a like service for Wakefield. MANNINGHAM v. HULL. Hull outplaye I their rivals at Manainehem, and won by three goals and five tries to one try. !ornerier eDale, Riff en. D-iecoll. and Jacques registered the tries, the Last-named also kicking tee goals. HALIFAX v. HUDDERSFIELD. One goal and a try to nil in favour of Halifax was the outcome of this eame on the winners ground. Nichol scored the try, which Frith converted. BRIMLEY v. HOLBECK. These fifteens met at Bramley, when the result of an rater., sting game was a draw, nothing being scored. LANCASHIRE " A " TEAMS CHAMPIONSHIP. LEIGH (A) V. WA.RRINGTON tA.) At Leigh, Warriegton started, and no return being mule, Ward van., n=inspleuoD9 with a good rub. Leigh had a grand chance to score, but the forwards kicked dead. Sefton scored for Leigh, Roberti failing at goal. Pennington dribbled over the Warrington line, but was robbed of the ball. Half-time :—Leigh. 1 try (3 points), Warrington nil. In the second half Warrington played up better, but were opposed by a strong defenee. A few nreutes from time, however, R Bate and Nelson got over the Leigh line, and won the match for Warrington by 2 tries to one. STOCKPORT (A) v. WIDNES (A.) At Stockport. Final : Widnes (A), 3 tries, Stock' port (A), nil. ROCHDALE HORIETS '' A" V. BROUGHTON RANGERS ii A.. At Rochdale. From the start the game Was contested in a spirited manner. the Hornets havine decidedly the best of matters Th mopson scored after a passing movement. Half-time : Hornets, 1 try ; Rangers, nil. The second half wasi characterised by the spirited play of the first half. Vaughan scored for the Hornets, Hiwards failing. The Hornets pressei to the close. Final :—Rochdale Hornets, six points; Broughton Ran- gers. nil. OLDHAM (A) V. TYLDESLEY (A). -At Oldham, before 2000, spectators. Oldham had a good team.and early on were able to score twice through</p>
