        <p>THE TERMENI OF WARRINGTON OM N IB USES. IMPORTANT AL'rERATIONS. At a meeting of the Watch Committee on Thurs- day,the annual inspection and licensing of hackney carriages plying for hire within the Borough vv ere" proceeded with. In order to relieve the overcrowd ing which at present exists at Market Gate owing to the increased vehicular traffic, itlwas decided that the termini of the 'buses should be altered and an effort made to prevent, as far as possible the 'bases from crossing and recrossing Market Gate. The alterations made are as follows : Terminus for Latchford : Lipton's corner in Bridge-street. Terminus for Stockton Heath : Vacant land at the corner of Bylands'-street. Terminus for Sankey Bridges: Corner of Bold- street. Terminus for Cemetery: C.)rner of Scotland- road. One of the Latchford 'buses will b 3 allowed to run , once every hour from the Central Station in order to meet tha Liverpool and Manchester express trains It is stated that the alterations will be the means nf relieving .the traffic at Market Gate to the extent of 40 'buses per hour. Tile alter- ations will come into effect on the first of Febra... rv. It is inteti&amp;d to provi&amp; a time table for the variou4 'buses and obviate if possible the present overlap- ping and inter mi tent running of 'buses. Another important alteration which will be inaugurat d on the same date win be the running of a pemuy 'bus to Stockton Heat h. .</p>
