        <p>MARRIAGES. MORTON—PEERS —January 12th at the Parish Church, War- rington, by the Rev. Canon Willis, John William Morton. to Sarah Ellen Peers. WHITHAM —BROOKE—At the Parish Church, Kirkburtort. near Huddersfield, by the Rev. G. Walton, Ethel Brooke., daughter of the late George Brooke, of Yew Tree. Kirithur- ton, to George Whitham of Manchester-road. Warrington on Thursday the 12th inst. DEATHS. BECKETT—January 6th. at Kean-street, Warrington, Maria Beckett, aged 62 years. HARRISON—January Bth, at Forster-street. Warrington, Wiliam Harrison, aged 2 years. WlLCOCK—January Bth, at Orford-lane, Warrington, Mary Ellen Wilcock, aged 41 year&amp; HARDMAN—January Bth. at Leicester-street, Waazington, Thomas Hardman, aged 38 years. WRlGHT—January 10th, at Knutsford-read; Warrington, Elizabeth Wright, aged 45 years. DENNEr —January 10th, at Garden-row, Warrington, Alfred Denney, aged 5 years. RUNCORN. CLARKE—On 12th lust, at 12. Okell-street, Jane, wife of Mr Daniel Clarke, aged 49 years. LLorn-12th 'dust. at 18, Norfolk-street, Elizabeth Ethel, daughter of Mr. Richard Lloyd, aged 2 years. BAVENSCRoFT —l4th inst, at 58. Cawdor-strefit. Mary, wife of Mr. Ralph Ravenscroft, aged 31 years. woonwenn-16th met, at 83. Shaw-street, 3lr. Peter Wood- ward waterman, aged 43 years. IN MEMORIAM. In loving memory of toy dear mother HANNau Otrnm, who fell asleep January 17th, 1297, aged Tek years. Qoae but not forgotten.</p>
